---
title: Subway's Chipotle Southwest sauce
description: We loved this sauce and then they retired it, so trying to recreate it
servings: 16
source: https://goodfooddiscoveries.com/chipotle-southwest-sauce-subway-copycat/#wpzoom-premium-recipe-card
image: https://goodfooddiscoveries.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/subway-chipotle-sauce-3-800x530.jpg
---

In a #blender, combine @mayonnaise{1/2%cup}(120g),  @ranch dressing{1/2%cup}(120g), @chipotle peppers{2%tbsp}(with adobo sauce, more to taste), @Worcestershire sauce{1%tsp}, @dijon mustard{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @onion powder{1%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @lime juice{2%tbsp}, @sugar{1%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp} until smooth.

Taste and adjust the spiciness by adding more @?chipotle peppers{} if needed.

Pour into a jar or air-tight container and keep refrigerated for up to two week.